pair<a, b> = [a, b]
; A generic instantiation used as a bare MEMBER type (`[pair<uint, tstr>]`): the anonymous instance
; (`PairU64Text`) must be registered + emitted, and the enclosing record's field bound to it, not
; dropped so the member dangles on a bare, never-emitted `Pair`. This is the last position of the
; generic-instantiation family to be closed (keyed members, rule RHSes, and homogeneous array
; elements already worked) — see tests/corpus/generic_array_element.cddl for the element position.
x = [pair<uint, tstr>]
; The SAME instantiation ALSO used under an occurrence (`[* pair<uint, tstr>]`): the member and the
; element positions register the identical instance ident (emitted as `PairU64Text`); this pins that the
; double registration is deterministic and yields one shared emitted struct.
y = [* pair<uint, tstr>]
